    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Ashton was founded in 1879 and has operated a post office since that same year.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ashton%2C_South_Dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town of Ashton was relocated five miles north in 1881 to align with the Milwaukee Road railroad line.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        2,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ashton%2C_South_Dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Ashton briefly served as the first county seat of Spink County before the title moved to Redfield in 1886.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/ashton_south_dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "A contentious election in 1886 nearly led to armed conflict over the location of the county seat.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/ashton_south_dakota"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Ashton developed into a quiet farming hub focused on livestock and grain production after losing its status as county seat.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
